\n\
Playing Forest now and Lieutenant: next turn if I draw/play Island, I have GWU for Katara the Fearless which doubles Ally triggers. Lieutenant is an Ally, Poxbearers is an Ally presumably (it creates Ally tokens; its types — \"Pretending Poxbearers\" likely is an Ally creature).\n\
\n\
Lieutenant on turn 2 gets value over time. Poxbearers is a better body immediately (2/1). But Lieutenant with more allies grows.\n\
\n\
Opponent has Raucous Audience (2/1 mana dork) and is on B/G.\n\
\n\
I think playing Forest and casting Earth King's Lieutenant is a solid tempo play. Actually wait — is it better to play Plains and cast Poxbearers for a 2/1? The 2/1 attacks into their 2/1 Audience... they probably don't block since Audience is a mana dork.\n\
\n\
Actually, let's think about sequencing for Katara the Fearless (GWU) on turn 3: I need Forest + Island + Plains by turn 3. If I play Forest now, then turn 3 play Island, I have Plains+Forest+Island = can cast Katara the Fearless. That's a strong curve: Lieutenant turn 2, Katara turn 3 (doubling Lieutenant's future triggers).\n\
\n\
