\n\
If I airbend Ostrich-Horse first, their only blocker is Long Feng 2/3. Then attack with Katara 5/5 (vigilance? Katara the Fearless doesn't say vigilance in text shown... the card reference shows just the trigger text, hmm, Katara the Fearless 3/3: \"If a triggered ability of an Ally you control triggers, that ability triggers an additional time.\" No vigilance listed), Poxbearers 4/3, Lieutenant 1/1.\n\
\n\
They block with Long Feng on something — kills Lieutenant maybe. Still get through ~9 damage. Opponent at 18 → 9.\n\
\n\
Alternatively Hakoda {3}{W} is a 3/5 vigilance that lets me cast Allies off the top. That's strong long-term. But Lieutenant + Ascension double-spell turn is more explosive and pumps the team.\n\
\n\
Let me reconsider: with Katara the Fearless, Earth King's Lieutenant ETB triggers twice (it's an Ally's triggered ability — Lieutenant is an Ally). So each other Ally gets two +1/+1 counters. Poxbearers 2/1 → 4/3. Katara 3/3 → 5/5. And Lieutenant enters as an Ally — its own \"whenever another Ally enters\" doesn't trigger for itself. But Katara the Fearless entering... no wait, Katara is already on the battlefield.\n\
\n\
Does Airbender Ascension's airbend count as... no, it's an enchantment, not a creature. Its ETB airbends; the quest counter ability triggers when creatures enter.\n\
\n\
Sequencing: Ascension first (airbend Ostrich-Horse), then Lieutenant (quest counter on Ascension → 1 counter, pumps team).\n\
\n\
Actually wait — is Katara, the Fearless an Ally? If so, when Lieutenant enters, does Katara's ability... Katara's ability is a static replacement-ish (\"triggers an additional time\"), not relevant. The question is whether Lieutenant's ETB triggers twice — yes, if Lieutenant is an Ally, which it is (\"Earth King's Lieutenant\" — Allies matter, its text references Ally creatures; the card should be Creature — Human Ally or similar).\n\
\n\
Also, does airbending Ostrich-Horse trigger Long Feng? No — airbend exiles, doesn't put into graveyard.\n\
