Alternatively airbend Long Feng to stop the counter engine? Ostrich-Horse is the bigger body. Airbend Ostrich-Horse.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but one consideration: airbend lets them recast for {2} less. Ostrich-Horse ETB mills 3 and maybe gets a land. Minor. The tempo is worth it — we're racing; they're at 18, we can hit hard this turn.\n\
\n\
Let me also consider: maybe just cast Lieutenant + Ascension and attack. Yes, that's the plan.\n\
\n\
Mana: Cast Airbender Ascension {1}{W}: tap Plains (W) + Island (U as generic 1)? Or use Plains+Plains for the {1}{W}? Then Lieutenant needs {G}{W}: Forest + remaining Plains. Let me plan: Ascension: Plains#1 (W) + Island (U for generic). Lieutenant: Forest (G) + Plains#2 (W). That works. Auto-tap should handle it.\n\
\n\
Cast Ascension first. Target Ostrich-Horse with airbend.\n\
\n\
Then cast Lieutenant. Then attack with Katara (5/5), Poxbearers (4/3), Lieutenant (1/1)? Lieutenant has trample. They block with Long Feng 2/3. If they block Poxbearers, Poxbearers dies → creates 1/1 Ally token → triggers Lieutenant's \"another Ally enters\" → Lieutenant gets +1/+1. Also token enters → quest counter on Ascension. Trade is fine.\n\
