      "thinking": "I cast Airbender Ascension and now I need to select a target for the airbend trigger. The plan was to airbend Ostrich-Horse. Airbending exiles the creature, and its owner can cast it for {2} as long as it remains exiled. Ostrich-Horse is their biggest creature (4/2). Exiling it removes a blocker and attacker.\n\
\n\
Wait, but if I airbend Ostrich-Horse, they can recast it for {2}... but they don't have {2} right now — all their lands are tapped. So it'll be exiled at least this turn, which lets my attack through. Also, when they recast it, they mill 3 again.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, airbend Long Feng (2/3). But Ostrich-Horse is the bigger threat/blocker.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — should I consider airbending my own creature? No, that doesn't make sense... Actually airbending my own creature could re-trigger ETB... Pretending Poxbearers has no ETB (only dies trigger). Katara the Fearless has no ETB. So no value there.\n\
\n\
Target Ostrich-Horse (p13).",
