\n\
South Pole Voyager ETB: Ally enters → Ascension gets 4th quest counter. Then at end step, Ascension can blink a creature. If I blink Earth King's Lieutenant, it re-enters and pumps all other Allies with +1/+1 counters (each other Ally gets a counter), and triggers Ascension again (5 counters), and triggers South Pole Voyager again (gain life, possibly draw if second time — wait, Voyager's ability: \"Whenever this or another Ally you control enters, you gain 1 life. If this is the second time this ability has resolved this turn, draw a card.\")\n\
\n\
Sequence if I cast Voyager:\n\
1. Voyager ETB: its own trigger (gain 1 life), Lieutenant trigger (+1/+1 counter on Lieutenant), Ascension trigger (4th counter).\n\
2. End step: Ascension blinks a creature. Best target: Earth King's Lieutenant — it re-enters, putting +1/+1 counters on each other Ally (Voyager becomes 3/3, token becomes 3/3), triggers Ascension (5 counters), triggers Voyager (second time — gain 1 life and draw a card!), triggers Lieutenant's own ETB... wait Lieutenant ETB puts counters on each OTHER Ally. Also when Lieutenant enters, Voyager's trigger resolves second time this turn → draw a card.\n\
\n\
That's great value. So casting Voyager now is clearly correct.\n\
\n\
