\n\
Should I consider holding Voyager to cast next turn alongside Katara, Water Tribe's Hope? Next turn I'd have 6 mana (assuming no land drop... actually I have a land drop next turn). Katara costs {2}{W}{U}{U} = 5 ~. With 6 lands I could cast Katara + Voyager. But casting Voyager now gives the blink value this turn (counters on team, draw a card, gain life). Also develops board. Definitely cast now.\n\
\n\
Let me also double check: does the end-step blink target \"up to one target creature you control\" — yes. Blinking Lieutenant is the best play. When Lieutenant re-enters: ETB trigger puts +1/+1 counter on each other Ally (token 2/2→3/3, Voyager 2/2→3/3). Ascension trigger: 5 counters. Voyager trigger: second resolution this turn → gain 1 life, draw a card.\n\
\n\
Wait — actually does Voyager's trigger count \"this is the second time this ability has resolved this turn\"? First resolution: Voyager's own ETB. Second: Lieutenant's blink ETB. Yes, second time → draw a card.\n\
\n\
Also note Hakoda could be cast? Hakoda is {3}{W} = 4 mana, I only have 2 untapped. No.\n\
\n\
So: cast South Pole Voyager, auto-tap Island + Plains.\n\
\n\
One consideration: which lands to tap. I want to keep flexibility? Nothing else to cast this turn. Auto-tap is fine.\n\
\n\
Then end step: choose blink target= Earth King's Lieutenant.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Voyager.",
