I'll go with the safe-ish option that keeps my preferred engine: single-block Swamp with Lieutenant? Or Voyager?\n\
\n\
Ugh, OK, final answer on which to keep. Let me think about the NEXT 2 turns concretely.\n\
\n\
Keep-Voyager line (Lt dies): T6: 6 mana (draw land) or 5. Cast Katara WTH (5): 3/3 + 1/1 token, Voyager gains 1 (15). End step: blink Voyager → gain 1 (16), draw 1. Board: Voyager 2/2, Token 2/2, Katara 3/3, 1/1. T7: 6-7 mana. Cast Hakoda (4) + whatever drawn. Blink Voyager again (gain 17, draw). I'm at 16-17 life with a growing board and 2 extra cards drawn. Their board: Long Feng 5/6, Swamp 4/4, Audience 2/1 + 1-2 new cards. This is a stable, winning trajectory — Voyager's life gain offsets their chip damage, card draw finds answers/gas, Hakoda button protects.\n\
\n\
Keep-Lieutenant line (Voyager dies): T6: cast Katara WTH: Lt → 4/4, token. End step: blink... Katara WTH (make another token, Lt → 5/5) or Lt (pump team). Board: Lt 5/5 trample, Token 2/2, Katara 3/3, 1/1, 1/1. T7: attack? Lt 5/5 into Long Feng 5/6 = Lt dies, no. Stall. Cast Hakoda. Board grows but no card draw, no life gain. They're chipping me with trample. I'm at 14 with no life gain engine. Their Swamp 4/4 + Long Feng 5/6 attack: I block with my 5 creatures... I can actually block everything: Lt on Long Feng (Lt 5/5 vs 5/6: Lt dies... no wait blocking: Lt 5/5 blocks Long Feng 5/6 trample: Lt deals 5 to Long Feng (survives 5/6 with 5 dmg), Long Feng deals 5 to Lt (5 toughness, dies), 0 trample (5 assigned to Lt = lethal). Trade Lt for nothing. Or Token + 1/1 on Long Feng (3 toughness, 5 power: 2 through, both die), etc. Chumping.\n\
\n\
Keep-Voyager line is more robust. Final: single-block Swamp with Earth King's Lieutenant. Take 5 → 14. Keep Voyager + Token + hand.\n\
\n\
Hmm, wait, actually, hmm, let me reconsider option 1 (double block) once more, because killing the Swamp AND keeping Voyager (if they choose to kill Lt) is the dream. But they choose — a smart opponent kills Voyager (the engine). Then I keep Lt (which I just argued is the weaker keep) but kill the Swamp. Is \"keep Lt + kill Swamp\" better than \"keep Voyager + Swamp lives\"? \n\
\n\
Keep Lt + Swamp dead: their board: Long Feng 6/7 trample, Audience 3/2 trample (pumped). My board: Lt 3/3 (2 dmg, heals), Token 2/2. Then T6 cast Katara WTH → Lt 4/4, etc. Their next attack: 6/7 + 3/2 = 9 trample-ish power vs my blockers. \n\
\n\
Keep Voyager + Swamp alive: their board: Long Feng 5/6, Swamp 4/4, Audience 2/1. My board: Voyager 2/2, Token 2/2 + card engine.\n\
\n\
I prefer keep-Voyager. The card engine out-values over time, and Swamp 4/4 is blockable/chippable later (Voyager gains life to offset).\n\
\n\
FINAL: Block Swamp (p15) with Earth King's Lieutenant (p3). Take 5 from Long Feng → 14 life.\n\
\n\
Oh wait, one more check — should I block Long Feng with Lieutenant instead to reduce Long Feng's damage? Block Long Feng (5/6 trample) with Lt 3/3: 3 assigned to Lt (lethal), 2 trample through. Lt dies. Swamp unblocked: 4. Total: 6 → 13. vs block Swamp: 5 → 14. Blocking Swamp is better (5 < 6). Yes.\n\
\n\
And block Swamp with Lt: Lt deals 3 to Swamp (4 toughness, survives, heals EOT). Fine.\n\
\n\
So: blockers=\"p3:p15\". Take 5, go to 14. Lieutenant dies.\n\
\n\
Also should I send a chat message? The instructions say chat at least once every 2 turn cycles, and respond to opponent messages. Opponent (PilotB) has been chatting: \"Time for the lands to join the fight. That Ascension of yours is building quite a board.\" I should reply. Let me send a chat message along with or before the block.\n\
\n\
Let me send a quick chat, then declare the block. Actually, order: I can send chat first, then choose_action. Both are tool calls; choose_action blocks until next decision. Let me do the chat first, then the block in the same response? The instructions say I can make multiple independent tool calls in the same block. The chat and the block are independent. But choose_action blocks... it's fine, I'll call both.\n\
\n\
Rationale for the block: Lieutenant chumps the 4/4 Swamp to keep me at 14 while preserving the Voyager + Airbender Ascension blink engine (card draw + life gain), which is my long-game plan against their big tramplers. Hakoda remains in hand as an indestructible button.\n\
\n\
Summary line: \"Opponent attacked with Long Feng 5/6 trample and the earthbent Swamp 4/4. I'm blocking the Swamp with Earth King's Lieutenant (it dies, no trample so nothing extra gets through), taking 5 from Long Feng to go to 14. Preserving South Pole Voyager for the Ascension blink engine.\"\n\
\n\
Let me write the chat: something like \"Nice earthbent Swamp — shame it's running into my Lieutenant. Enjoy the land back.\" Something playful acknowledging their engine.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — if I block the Swamp with just Lieutenant, the Swamp does NOT die (takes 3, survives). So the chat shouldn't say \"enjoy the land back.\" Let me adjust: \"Long Feng's looking scary, but my Ascension engine's just getting started — Voyager's about to draw me a boatload.\"\n\
\n\
