\n\
Then end step: Airbender Ascension blinks a creature. If I blink Katara, she re-enters, makes another token, Voyager triggers twice more (gain 1, then gain 1 + draw). That's strong.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, cast Hakoda {3}{W}: 3/5 vigilance, leaves 1 mana up (G or U). Hakoda is an Ally? \"Hakoda, Selfless Commander\" — likely Human Ally? His ability: \"You may cast Ally spells from the top of your library.\" Sacrifice: team +0/+5 and indestructible. Hakoda entering triggers Voyager (gain 1) and Ascension counter. Then I still have 1 mana, can't cast Katara (needs 5).\n\
\n\
Which is better? Let me think about the board. Opponent has Long Feng 5/6 trample, Swamp 4/4, Raucous Audience 2/1. Their Earthbender Ascension at 5 counters — landfall: when they play a land, put a quest counter, and if 4+, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature and it gains trample. So every land drop pumps a creature and gives trample. Long Feng grows whenever another creature or land they control dies... actually \"whenever another creature you control or a land you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\"\n\
