      "reasoning": "All their creatures (Long Feng, Swamp land-creature, Raucous Audience) are tapped from their attack, so nobody can block. Swinging with both the 2/2 token and South Pole Voyager for 4 free damage (14→10), then I'll blink Katara in the end step for another token + Voyager triggers.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the board state.\n\
\n\
My board (PilotA), 16 life:\n\
- Airbender Ascension (7 quest counters)\n\
- Ally Token 2/2 (can attack)\n\
- Ally Token 1/1 (sick — just created by Katara's ETB, can't attack)\n\
- Forest (tapped), Island (tapped), North Pole Gates (tapped), Plains (tapped), Plains (tapped)\n\
- Katara, Water Tribe's Hope 3/3 (sick)\n\
- South Pole Voyager 2/2\n\
\n\
Opponent (PilotB), 14 life:\n\
- Ba Sing Se (tapped), Foggy Bottom Swamp, Forest (tapped), Forest, Omashu City, Swamp\n\
- Earthbender Ascension (5 quest counters)\n\
- Long Feng 5/6 (tapped)\n\
- Raucous Audience 2/1 (tapped)\n\
- Swamp 4/4 land creature (tapped)\n\
\n\
All their creatures are tapped! Long Feng 5/6 tapped, Raucous Audience tapped, Swamp 4/4 tapped. So they have no blockers.\n\
\n\
Wait — the Swamp 4/4 land creature: is it tapped? It says \"Swamp 4/4 (tapped, 4 +1/+1 counters)\". Yes, tapped.\n\
\n\
So attacking with Ally Token 2/2 and South Pole Voyager 2/2 = 4 damage, unblockable. They go from 14 to 10.\n\
\n\
Should I attack with both? Voyager is my blink engine piece. But there are no blockers, so no risk. Attack with both for 4 damage.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — after combat, Airbender Ascension's end-step trigger will blink something. Let me think about the plan: blink Katara, Water Tribe's Hope → she ETBs again, creates another token, triggers Voyager twice (life + draw). That's the plan.\n\
\n\
But first, combat: attack with both creatures since all their blockers are tapped. 4 damage,they go to 10.\n\
\n\
Let me attack with all available (p77 and p84).",
