        "content": "{\"analysis\":\"The list is internally consistent: 23 spells (17 creatures, 6 non-creatures), the curve and pip counts check out, and the build is coherent — a white-based Ally deck (Hakoda, South Pole Voyager, Kyoshi Warriors, Jeong Jeong's Deserters, Pretending Poxbearers, Earth King's Lieutenants, Katara the Fearless as payoffs) splashing blue via North Pole Gates/Meditation Pools for Otter-Penguin, Kuruk, Boomerang Basics and Katara, Water Tribe's Hope, plus a light green splash via Kyoshi Village/Meditation Pools for the two Earth King's Lieutenants and Katara, the Fearless. Removal suite (Razor Rings, Path to Redemption, Airbender Ascension, Airbending Lesson, Boomerang Basics) is adequate, and the double-blue cards are 4-5 mana so the modest blue source count is acceptable. Appa and Katara WTH give late-game top end while the heavy 2-drop slot supports the aggressive Ally plan. The green splash is justified by four strong Ally payoffs and is supported by two green-producing dual lands. Alternatives considered (Avatar's Wrath, Compassionate Healer, First-Time Flyer, Crashing Wave) don't clearly improve the synergy core, and red cards (Sokka Tenacious Tactician, Wandering Musicians) would strain the mana into a fourth color. This is the deck I intended.\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"chosen_spells\":[\"Hakoda, Selfless Commander\",\"Water Tribe Captain\",\"Kyoshi Warriors\",\"Kyoshi Warriors\",\"Appa, Loyal Sky Bison\",\"South Pole Voyager\",\"Momo, Playful Pet\",\"Jeong Jeong's Deserters\",\"Jeong Jeong's Deserters\",\"Curious Farm Animals\",\"Pretending Poxbearers\",\"Katara, the Fearless\",\"Katara, Water Tribe's Hope\",\"Sokka, Lateral Strategist\",\"Earth King's Lieutenant\",\"Earth King's Lieutenant\",\"Otter-Penguin\",\"Razor Rings\",\"Path to Redemption\",\"Airbender Ascension\",\"Airbending Lesson\",\"The Legend of Kuruk\",\"Boomerang Basics\"]}",
